// @exit 134
// @stderr-contains panic: the task started at tasks_launch_cancelled.ens:10 threw 'Cancelled' although nothing cancelled it, and nothing awaits a task started with 'launch', so nothing would handle the error. Catch 'Cancelled' inside its body
// A launched task ends quietly on a 'Cancelled' only when it was cancelled, so one that throws it
// unasked aborts the program, naming the line that started it.
import @std.tasks;
import Cancelled from @std.tasks;

main() -> int {
    tasks.scope((scope) -> {
        scope.launch(() -> {
            throw new Cancelled();
        });
    });
    return 0;
}
